# Who has to review a change to the dependency watch.
#
# **This file does nothing on its own.** CODEOWNERS makes GitHub request a review
# automatically, but it only *requires* one when branch protection on `master` has
# "Require review from Code Owners" turned on. That setting is Patrick's to make, in the
# repository settings, and until he does this file is a request rather than a rule.
#
# Why these paths and not others. A pull request is checked by its own copy of the tools and
# its own copy of the allowlist, so a pull request can weaken the gate it is being judged by:
# raise the age limit, add its own allowlist entry, or edit the check. The weekly run on
# `master` catches that a week later, and a required review catches it before it merges.
# These four paths are the whole of that surface.

# The checks themselves, and their tests.
/tools/                         @patrickdorival

# What the checks knowingly let through, and until when.
/dependency-allowlist.toml      @patrickdorival

# The workflows, including the one the dependency watch runs in.
/.github/workflows/             @patrickdorival

# The update bot's configuration, including the TypeScript major-version ignore.
/.github/dependabot.yml         @patrickdorival

# This file.
/.github/CODEOWNERS             @patrickdorival
